==German==
[[File:Fourrékoeken.jpg|thumb|{{l|de||'''Kekse'''}}]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Cakes||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|non|gem-pro}}
{{bor+|de|en|cakes}}, 1900s. Popularized by German food company {{w|Bahlsen}} which changed the brand name of their biscuits from ''Leibniz-Cakes'' to ''Leibniz-Keks'' in 1911; at the time, the plural was also {{m|de||Keks}}. Compare {{cog|da|kiks}}, {{cog|et|keeks}}, {{cog|fo|keks}}, {{cog|fi|keksi}}, {{cog|is|kex}}, {{cog|no|kjeks}}, and {{cog|sv|kex}}, all ‘cookie, biscuit, cracker’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/keːks/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Keks.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m:n,es,e}}

# [[cookie]] {{qualifier|US}}, [[biscuit]] {{qualifier|UK}}
#: {{syn|de|Biskuit|Plätzchen}}
#* {{quote-book|de|year=1924|author=w:Theodor Birt|title=Auf Reisen: ein Ferienbuch|page=101
|passage={{l|de||Da sitzt leibhaftig Schillers Schwester: eine rötliche Blondine, noch ganz jung, die vor mir aus dem Fenster guckt und einen '''Keks''' zerbeißt.}}
|translation=Schiller’s sister incarnate is sitting there: a strawberry blonde, still very young, looking out of the window in front of me and biting into a '''cookie'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|de|year=1935|author=Hungarian Chamber of Commerce and Industry|title=Ungarns Handel und Industrie im Jahre 1935|page=123
|passage={{l|de||Immer breitere Publikumsschichten gehen zum Konsum der Fabriks'''keks'''sorten über, die qualitativ besser und billiger sind, als die im Privathaushalt hergestellten '''Kekse'''.}}
|translation=Ever broader classes of the public are going over to the consumption of factory-made '''cookie''' types that are qualitatively better and cheaper than '''cookies''' made in private homes.}}
#* '''1968,''' Arbeitsgemeinschaft Getreideforschung, ''Brot und Gebäck'', volumes 22-24, p.&nbsp;45:
#*: {{quote|de|In Wirklichkeit sind jedoch die atmosphärischen Ofenverhältnisse, sofern sie überhaupt bekannt sein können, nicht direkt bestimmend für die backtechnische Entwicklung des Brotes oder '''Kekses'''.|In reality, however, the atmospheric conditions in the oven, to the extent they can be known at all, do not directly determine the baking development of the bread or '''cookie'''.}}

====Usage notes====
The word is always masculine in northern and central Germany. In the southern half of the language area it is often neuter.

